#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hq-auth — which agent may use which shared service, and with which account.

  hq-auth ls                              every agent: the services it needs, its grant, whether the secrets resolve
  hq-auth grant <agent> <service> <profile>   let an agent use a service as that profile (e.g. notion/library);
                                          several agents as a,b,c, or --all for every agent whose needs list it;
                                          several profiles as p1,p2 (the bridge: one bot each, telegram/hq,telegram/x)
  hq-auth granted [--for AGENT] <service> the profiles granted, one per line
  hq-auth revoke <agent> <service>
  hq-auth set <profile> <VAR>             store a secret in the macOS Keychain (prompts; never echoed) and point
                                          the profile at it
  hq-auth mcp-config <agent>              the --mcp-config JSON for an agent's granted MCP services (bin/hq uses it)
  hq-auth exec [--for AGENT] <service> -- CMD...   run CMD with that service's secrets in its environment only
  hq-auth get  [--for AGENT] [--profile P] <service> <VAR>   print one secret, for an agent's own tool to call;
                                          --profile picks one of several granted profiles
  hq-auth env  <agent> <service> [VAR=value | VAR=]  this agent's own settings for a service (not secrets), e.g.
                                          hq-auth env personal jev-browser JEV_BROWSER_HEADED=1; VAR= drops one
  hq-auth browser <name> [<browser>]      a browser profile (its logins, in ~/.hq/browsers/<name>) and the browser
                                          that made it: chrome, chromium, msedge, firefox, or an app's path

People (who may use which agent, and how; the run's person is HQ_PERSON, unset = the owner):
  hq-auth people [ID ...] [--matrix]      each person: their accounts, the profiles they own, every agent they can
                                          reach (own row, everyone row, helper) with its mode, and the account each
                                          service would really use in their runs; ID for one person in full (the
                                          owner's agents too); --matrix: agents × people at a glance
  hq-auth person <id> [name=.. lang=.. tz=.. owner] [--rm]   a person; `owner` marks you (one owner)
  hq-auth person <id> id=<new>            rename: memberships, grants, owned profiles and invites come along; the
                                          old id stays as an alias (bridge threads they started stay theirs)
  hq-auth handle <id> <platform> <user-id> | --rm   the person's account on a platform (numeric id, not a username)
  hq-auth invite <id> [minutes]           a one-time code (default 15 minutes); they send /link CODE to the bridge
  hq-auth link <platform> <user-id> <code>   bind that account to the code's person (the bridge calls it)
  hq-auth whois <platform> <user-id>      the person behind an account, or exit 1
  hq-auth who <platform> <user-id>        the same as JSON for the bridge: {person, owner, was, owner_id,
                                          owner_linked}; person null when no one is linked
  hq-auth preset <name> [mode=.. deny=a,b] [--trusted] [--rm]   a named bundle of permissions memberships point at
  hq-auth member <agent>[,..] <id> [preset=.. mode=.. deny=.. model=.. helpers=a,b budget=USD env.VAR=..] [--trusted] [--rm]
                                          let a person use an agent, with their own settings on top of the agent's;
                                          <id> '*' is everyone hq knows (not unknown senders); their own row wins.
                                          mode=bypassPermissions is a free shell on this Mac as you: refused unless
                                          --trusted (a row or preset without it runs in default mode).
                                          budget=20: at most $20 a calendar month of their runs of that agent
                                          (helpers they reach through it included; hq cost people shows it)
  hq-auth owner <profile> <id>|-|default  the profile is that person's (their logins, their calendar); - = shared;
                                          default: logins and browser profiles are the owner's, keys and bots shared
  hq-auth share <profile> <id>[,..] [--rm]   it stays its owner's, and these people's runs may use it too (through
                                          the agents granted it that they may use)
  hq-auth may <id> <agent> [--via AGENT]  exit 0 if the person may use the agent (--via: called as AGENT's helper)
  hq-auth resolve <agent> [--person ID] [--via AGENT]   the run's effective person settings, as JSON (bin/hq uses it)

Three layers, so sharing an agent never shares an account:
  kernel/services/<name>.json   what a service is: kind (mcp | cli | login), how to start it, which env vars it needs.
                                In the repo; no secrets.
  agents/<a>/capabilities.yaml  `needs: [service, ...]`: what the agent asks for. Part of the agent package.
  ~/.hq/secrets/auth.json      profiles (an account: where each secret comes from) and grants (agent → service →
                                profile). Yours alone, never in the repo. Holds references, not secret values.
                                Also env (agent → service → VAR: value): plain settings that override the
                                service's own env for that agent only.

People are tables in the same file, each fact in one place: people (who someone is, their handles), presets
(named permissions), members (agent → person → preset and overrides: access is the row existing) and grants keyed
`<agent>@<person>` for a person's own accounts, tried before the agent's. A profile with "person" is that person's:
a run for anyone else never gets it, whatever the grants say. The owner may use every agent with no membership.

Browser profiles: logins belong to a browser profile, not to a tool, so every browser tool an agent has (each
service with "browsers" in its json) opens the agent's one profile: `hq-auth grant <agent> browser browser/<name>`;
without a grant, the agent's own (browser/<agent>). Agents granted the same profile share its logins, though only
one run can have it open at a time. A service gets $HQ_BROWSER and $HQ_BROWSER_PROFILE for its env and args, and
is left out of a run when it can't drive the profile's browser (a profile is only ever opened by the browser that
made it).

Secret sources in a profile: "keychain:SERVICE#ACCOUNT", "env-file:PATH#VAR", "env:VAR". A `login` service (codex,
a Chrome profile) has no secrets here: the tool keeps its own login, and the grant only says who may use it.

The agent comes from HQ_AGENT (set by bin/hq) or --for (an agent's own tool naming its owner). This is least
privilege between cooperating agents, not a sandbox: an agent with a shell can still read files it can see.
"""
import getpass
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

HQ = Path(os.environ.get('HQ_ROOT') or os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(
    os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.environ.get('PWD') or os.getcwd(), sys.argv[0])))))
SERVICES = HQ / 'services'

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), '..', 'lib'))
from hq_paths import paths  # noqa: E402  the one place that knows where hq's folders are
STATE_ROOT, AGENTS = paths()['HQ_STATE'], paths()['HQ_AGENTS']  # <home>/state, <home>/agents


def agent_dirs():
    out = {}
    for root in (AGENTS, HQ / 'agents'):
        for d in sorted(root.iterdir()) if root.is_dir() else []:
            pkg = d / 'role' if (d / 'role' / 'agent.md').is_file() else d   # role/ next to the agent's life
            if not d.name.startswith('.') and (pkg / 'agent.md').is_file():
                out.setdefault(d.name, pkg)
    return out
AUTH = Path(os.environ.get('HQ_AUTH') or paths()['HQ_SECRETS'] / 'auth.json')
LOG = AUTH.with_name('auth.log')   # every secret handed out: when, to whom, for which service; never the value


def die(msg, code=1):
    print(f'hq-auth: {msg}', file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


def load_auth():
    try:
        data = json.loads(AUTH.read_text())
    except FileNotFoundError:
        data = {}
    except ValueError as e:
        die(f'{AUTH}: invalid JSON ({e})')
    for table in ('profiles', 'grants', 'env', 'people', 'presets', 'members', 'invites'):
        data.setdefault(table, {})
    return data


def save_auth(data):
    AUTH.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = AUTH.with_name(AUTH.name + '.tmp')
    now = time.time()
    data['invites'] = {c: i for c, i in data.get('invites', {}).items() if i.get('expires', 0) > now}
    data = {k: v for k, v in data.items() if v or k in ('profiles', 'grants', 'env')}   # no empty people tables
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2) + '\n')
    os.chmod(tmp, 0o600)
    tmp.rename(AUTH)


def service_file(name):
    """kernel/services/<name>.json, else one an installed agent brings in its role's services/ (an agent shared by
    someone else can carry the definition of a service the kernel doesn't have)."""
    f = SERVICES / f'{name}.json'
    if f.is_file():
        return f
    for pkg in agent_dirs().values():
        if (pkg / 'services' / f'{name}.json').is_file():
            return pkg / 'services' / f'{name}.json'
    return None


def service(name):
    f = service_file(name)
    if not f:
        die(f"no service '{name}' (kernel/services/, or an agent's services/)")
    return json.loads(f.read_text())


def needs(agent):
    f = agent_dirs().get(agent, AGENTS / agent) / 'capabilities.yaml'
    m = re.search(r'^needs:\s*\[([^\]]*)\]', f.read_text(), re.M) if f.exists() else None
    return [s.strip() for s in m.group(1).split(',') if s.strip()] if m else []


def agents():
    return sorted(agent_dirs())


def owner(auth):
    return next((p for p, v in auth['people'].items() if v.get('owner')), None)


def acting(auth):
    """The person this run works for: HQ_PERSON, set by the entry point (the bridge, a schedule) and inherited by
    every helper; unset is the owner."""
    return canonical(auth, os.environ.get('HQ_PERSON') or owner(auth) or '')


def is_owner(auth, person):
    return not person or person == owner(auth)


EVERYONE = '*'   # a membership row for every person hq knows (never an unknown sender); a person's own row wins


def row_of(auth, agent, person):
    """The person's membership of agent: their own row, else the agent's `*` row, else None."""
    rows = auth['members'].get(agent, {})
    return rows.get(person, rows.get(EVERYONE))


def may(auth, person, agent, via=None):
    """(allowed, why). Access is a membership row; a helper is allowed when the caller's membership lists it."""
    person = canonical(auth, person)
    if is_owner(auth, person):
        return True, 'owner'
    if person not in auth['people']:
        return False, f"'{person}' is not a person in hq (hq-auth people)"
    if row_of(auth, agent, person) is not None:
        return True, 'member' if person in auth['members'].get(agent, {}) else 'member (everyone)'
    if via and agent in (row_of(auth, via, person) or {}).get('helpers', []):
        return True, f'helper of {via}'
    return False, f'{person} may not use {agent}' + (f' (not in their {via} helpers)' if via else '')


SHARED = '*'      # a profile's person: shared on purpose, even for a service whose profiles are personal


def personal(svc):
    """Whether a service's profiles belong to someone unless marked shared: logins (a Chrome profile, a ChatGPT
    login) and browser profiles are; API keys and bots aren't. A service json can say "personal": true or false."""
    f = service_file(svc)
    spec = json.loads(f.read_text()) if f else {}
    return spec.get('personal', spec.get('kind') in ('login', 'browser'))


def owner_of(auth, profile):
    """Whose a profile is: its "person", else the owner's when its service is personal, else no one's (shared).
    With no owner named yet, "the owner" still owns it, so other people's runs are refused all the same."""
    belongs = auth['profiles'].get(profile, {}).get('person')
    if belongs == SHARED:
        return None
    if belongs:
        return belongs
    return (owner(auth) or 'the owner') if personal(profile.split('/', 1)[0]) else None


def granted(auth, agent, svc, person=None):
    """(profile, why not, refused): the person's own grant (<agent>@<person>) first, then the agent's. A profile that belongs
    to someone else is never handed over, so a missing personal grant can't fall back to another person's account."""
    person = acting(auth) if person is None else person
    profile = (auth['grants'].get(f'{agent}@{person}', {}).get(svc) if person else None) \
        or auth['grants'].get(agent, {}).get(svc)
    if isinstance(profile, list):   # several (the bridge's bots): the first, unless the caller picks one (--profile)
        pick = os.environ.get('HQ_AUTH_PROFILE')
        profile = pick if pick in profile else None if pick else (profile[0] if profile else None)
    if not profile:
        return None, f'{agent} has no grant for {svc} (hq-auth grant {agent} {svc} <profile>)', False
    belongs = owner_of(auth, profile)
    lent = auth['profiles'].get(profile, {}).get('with', [])
    if belongs and person and belongs != person and canonical(auth, person) not in lent:   # owner runs: never refused
        return None, (f'{profile} is {belongs}\'s and this run is for {person or "no one"} '
                      f'(hq-auth grant {agent}@{person} {svc} <their profile>)'), True
    return profile, '', False


def grant_for(auth, agent, svc):
    """The profile name this agent may use for svc, or exit with why not."""
    if not agent:
        die(f'who is asking for {svc}? (HQ_AGENT is not set; tools pass --for <agent>)')
    profile, why, _ = granted(auth, agent, svc)
    if not profile:
        die(why)
    return profile


def resolve_ref(ref):
    kind, _, rest = ref.partition(':')
    if kind == 'env':
        return os.environ.get(rest)
    if kind == 'env-file':
        path, _, var = rest.partition('#')
        try:
            for line in Path(os.path.expanduser(path)).read_text().splitlines():
                k, sep, v = re.sub(r'^export\s+', '', line.strip()).partition('=')
                if sep and k.strip() == var:
                    return v.strip().strip('"\'')
        except OSError:
            return None
        return None
    if kind == 'keychain':
        svc, _, account = rest.partition('#')
        try:   # a locked keychain or an access prompt must not hang a headless run
            r = subprocess.run(['security', 'find-generic-password', '-s', svc, '-a', account, '-w'],
                               capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            return None
        return r.stdout.rstrip('\n') if r.returncode == 0 else None
    return None


def secrets(auth, svc, profile):
    """{VAR: value} for every secret the service needs, from the profile. Exits if one is missing."""
    refs = auth['profiles'].get(profile)
    if refs is None:
        die(f"no profile '{profile}' in {AUTH}")
    out = {}
    for var in service(svc).get('secrets', []):
        ref = refs.get(var)
        value = resolve_ref(ref) if ref else None
        if not value:
            die(f'{profile}: {var} does not resolve ({ref or "not set"}; hq-auth set {profile} {var})')
        out[var] = value
    return out


def browser_profile(auth, agent):
    """(profile name, browser, folder) of the browser profile this agent's browser tools open. Without a grant, the
    agent's own; for someone other than the owner, one of their own (the agent's own holds the owner's logins).
    Exits when the granted profile is someone else's."""
    person = acting(auth)
    name, why, refused = granted(auth, agent, 'browser')
    if refused:
        die(why)
    name = name or (f'browser/{agent}' if is_owner(auth, person) else f'browser/{agent}-{person}')
    return name, auth['profiles'].get(name, {}).get('browser'), paths()['HQ_MACHINE'] / 'browsers' / name.split('/', 1)[1]


def drives(spec, browser):
    """Whether a browser service can run that browser (an app path counts when it lists "path")."""
    can = spec.get('browsers', [])
    return browser in can or ('path' in can and '/' in browser)


def settings(auth, agent, svc):
    """The service's env with this agent's own overrides on top; $HQ_AGENT in a value is this agent, $HQ_BROWSER
    and $HQ_BROWSER_PROFILE its browser profile. Exits when a browser service can't drive that profile's browser."""
    os.environ['HQ_AGENT'] = agent
    for k, v in paths().items():   # $HQ_MACHINE and the rest, also when hq-auth runs on its own
        os.environ.setdefault(k, str(v))
    spec = service(svc)
    if spec.get('browsers'):
        name, browser, folder = browser_profile(auth, agent)
        browser = browser or spec['browsers'][0]   # a new profile starts in the service's first browser
        if not drives(spec, browser):
            die(f'{svc} can\'t drive {browser}, the browser of {name} ({agent}\'s profile; hq-auth browser)')
        folder.parent.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)   # logins: this user only
        os.environ.update(HQ_BROWSER=browser, HQ_BROWSER_PROFILE=str(folder))
    env = {**spec.get('mcp', {}).get('env', {}), **auth['env'].get(agent, {}).get(svc, {})}
    return {k: expand(v) for k, v in env.items()}


def uses_browser(agent):
    return any(service_file(s) and service(s).get('browsers') for s in needs(agent))


def audit(agent, svc, profile, how):
    """One line per secret handed out. --for can name any agent, so the log records who was really running too."""
    try:
        with open(LOG, 'a') as f:
            f.write(f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')}\t{how}\t{svc}\t{profile}\tfor={agent}"
                    f"\trun={os.environ.get('HQ_AGENT', '-')}\tppid={os.getppid()}"
                    f"\tperson={os.environ.get('HQ_PERSON') or 'owner'}\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


def expand(text):
    return os.path.expandvars(os.path.expanduser(text)) if isinstance(text, str) else text


def take_for(args):
    agent = os.environ.get('HQ_AGENT', '')
    if args[:1] == ['--for']:
        agent, args = args[1], args[2:]
    return agent, args


def cmd_ls():
    auth = load_auth()
    for agent in agents():
        wanted = needs(agent)
        granted = auth['grants'].get(agent, {})
        if not wanted and not granted:
            continue
        print(agent)
        for svc, profile in sorted((s, p) for s in (set(wanted) | set(granted)) - {'browser'}   # browser: own line
                                   for p in (granted.get(s) if isinstance(granted.get(s), list) else [granted.get(s)])):
            if not profile:
                print(f'  {svc:<14} NOT GRANTED')
                continue
            note = '' if svc in wanted else '  (granted, not in needs)'
            refs = auth['profiles'].get(profile)
            try:
                missing = [v for v in service(svc).get('secrets', [])
                           if not (refs and refs.get(v) and resolve_ref(refs[v]))]
            except SystemExit:
                missing = ['unknown service']
            status = 'ok' if refs is not None and not missing else \
                'no such profile' if refs is None else 'missing ' + ', '.join(missing)
            print(f'  {svc:<14} {profile:<24} {status}{note}')
            for var, value in auth['env'].get(agent, {}).get(svc, {}).items():
                print(f'  {"":<14} {var}={value}')
        if uses_browser(agent) or 'browser' in granted:
            name, browser, folder = browser_profile(auth, agent)
            own = '' if 'browser' in granted else '  (its own; no browser grant)'
            print(f'  {"browser":<14} {name:<24} {browser or "not set"}, ~/{folder.relative_to(Path.home())}{own}')


def cmd_mcp_config(agent):
    auth = load_auth()
    servers = {}
    for svc in needs(agent):
        spec = service(svc)
        if spec.get('kind') != 'mcp':
            continue
        profile, why, refused = granted(auth, agent, svc)
        if not profile:
            print(f'hq: {agent}: {svc} left out this run: {why}' if refused else
                  f'hq: {agent} needs {svc} but has no grant; running without it '
                  f'(hq-auth grant {agent} {svc} <profile>)', file=sys.stderr)
            continue
        try:
            secrets(auth, svc, profile)    # skip a server whose secrets don't resolve instead of failing at start
        except SystemExit:
            print(f'hq: {agent}: {svc} skipped this run, its secrets don\'t resolve (hq-auth ls)', file=sys.stderr)
            continue
        try:
            env = settings(auth, agent, svc)   # also skip a browser tool that can't drive the agent's profile
        except SystemExit:
            print(f'hq: {agent}: {svc} skipped this run', file=sys.stderr)
            continue
        mcp = spec['mcp']
        if os.environ.get('HQ_PERSON'):
            env['HQ_PERSON'] = os.environ['HQ_PERSON']   # the server's own hq-auth exec decides for the same person
        # Secrets are resolved when the server starts, inside hq-auth exec, so they never land in a config file
        # or in the agent's own environment.
        servers[svc] = {
            'command': str(HQ / 'bin' / 'hq-auth'),
            'args': ['exec', '--for', agent, svc, '--', mcp['command'], *[expand(a) for a in mcp.get('args', [])]],
            'env': env,
        }
    print(json.dumps({'mcpServers': servers}))


def cmd_exec(args):
    agent, args = take_for(args)
    if len(args) < 3 or args[1] != '--':
        die('exec [--for AGENT] <service> -- CMD...', 2)
    svc, cmd = args[0], args[2:]
    auth = load_auth()
    profile = grant_for(auth, agent, svc)
    env = {**os.environ, **settings(auth, agent, svc), **secrets(auth, svc, profile)}
    audit(agent, svc, profile, 'exec')
    os.execvpe(cmd[0], cmd, env)


def cmd_get(args):
    agent, args = take_for(args)
    if args[:1] == ['--profile']:
        os.environ['HQ_AUTH_PROFILE'], args = args[1], args[2:]
    if len(args) != 2:
        die('get [--for AGENT] <service> <VAR>', 2)
    svc, var = args
    auth = load_auth()
    if var not in service(svc).get('secrets', []):
        die(f'{svc} declares no secret {var}')
    profile = grant_for(auth, agent, svc)
    value = secrets(auth, svc, profile)[var]
    audit(agent, svc, profile, f'get {var}')
    print(value)


def cmd_set(profile, var):
    if '/' not in profile:
        die('profiles are named <service>/<account>, e.g. notion/library', 2)
    if var not in service(profile.split('/', 1)[0]).get('secrets', []):
        die(f'{profile.split("/", 1)[0]} declares no secret {var}')
    value = getpass.getpass(f'{profile} {var}: ')
    if not value:
        die('nothing entered; unchanged')
    kc = f'hq/{profile}'
    r = subprocess.run(['security', 'add-generic-password', '-U', '-s', kc, '-a', var, '-w', value],
                       capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        die(f'keychain: {r.stderr.strip()}')
    auth = load_auth()
    auth['profiles'].setdefault(profile, {})[var] = f'keychain:{kc}#{var}'
    save_auth(auth)
    print(f'stored in Keychain as {kc} / {var}; {profile} now reads it from there')


# A membership with no preset is a guest's. `default` mode in a one-shot run means only what the agent's own
# settings allow runs (house's own tool, not any shell command); auth.json presets of the same name replace these.
PRESETS = {'guest': {'mode': 'default'}, 'member': {'mode': 'acceptEdits'}}
# Modes that run any command without asking: a free shell on this Mac, as the owner. Only the owner has one, unless
# a membership or preset was set with --trusted.
FREE_SHELL = {'bypassPermissions'}


def preset(auth, name):
    return auth['presets'].get(name) or PRESETS.get(name) or die(f"no preset '{name}' (hq-auth preset {name} mode=..)")


def resolve(auth, agent, person, via=None):
    """What a run of agent for person gets: whether it may run, and the person's settings over the agent's. A helper
    reached through the caller's helpers list runs with the caller's membership, so calling one never loosens it."""
    person = canonical(auth, person)
    ok, why = may(auth, person, agent, via)
    me = auth['people'].get(person, {})
    out = {'person': person, 'owner': is_owner(auth, person), 'allowed': ok, 'why': why,
           **{k: me[k] for k in ('name', 'lang', 'tz') if k in me}}
    if not ok or out['owner']:
        return out
    row = row_of(auth, agent, person)
    if row is None:
        row = row_of(auth, via, person)
    p = preset(auth, row.get('preset', 'guest'))
    out.update(preset=row.get('preset', 'guest'), mode=mode_of(row, p),
               deny=list(dict.fromkeys(p.get('deny', []) + row.get('deny', []))),
               model=row.get('model', ''), env=row.get('env', {}), helpers=row.get('helpers', []),
               budget=row.get('budget', ''), budget_agent=agent if row_of(auth, agent, person) is not None else via,
               was=auth['people'].get(person, {}).get('was', []))
    return out


def mode_of(row, p):
    """The membership's mode; a free shell set without --trusted (say, by hand in auth.json) falls back to default."""
    mode = row.get('mode') or p.get('mode', 'default')
    trusted = row.get('trusted') if row.get('mode') else p.get('trusted')
    return 'default' if mode in FREE_SHELL and not trusted else mode


def check_free_shell(mode, flags, what):
    if mode in FREE_SHELL and '--trusted' not in flags:
        die(f'{what}: mode={mode} runs any command on this Mac as you, unasked. Add --trusted if you mean it', 2)


def pairs(args, allowed):
    """key=value arguments, `--rm` and bare flags, checked against the keys a command takes."""
    out, flags = {}, set()
    for a in args:
        k, eq, v = a.partition('=')
        if not eq:
            flags.add(a)
            continue
        if k not in allowed and not (k.startswith('env.') and 'env.' in allowed):
            die(f'unknown setting {k} (takes {", ".join(sorted(allowed))})', 2)
        out[k] = v
    return out, flags


def need_person(auth, pid):
    if pid not in auth['people']:
        die(f"no person '{pid}' (hq-auth person {pid} name=..)")


def services_of(auth, agent, person):
    """Every service a run of agent could be handed: its needs, its grants and the person's own grants."""
    out = set(needs(agent)) | set(auth['grants'].get(agent, {})) | set(auth['grants'].get(f'{agent}@{person}', {}))
    if uses_browser(agent):
        out.add('browser')
    return sorted(out)


def access(auth, person):
    """[(agent, how, settings)]: every agent the person can reach. how: owner, own, everyone, or helper of X."""
    if is_owner(auth, person):
        return [(a, 'owner', {}) for a in agents()]
    out, seen = [], set()
    for agent in agents():
        rows = auth['members'].get(agent, {})
        if person in rows or EVERYONE in rows:
            out.append((agent, 'own' if person in rows else 'everyone', resolve(auth, agent, person)))
            seen.add(agent)
    for agent, _, r in list(out):
        for h in r.get('helpers', []):
            if h not in seen and h in agent_dirs():
                out.append((h, f'helper of {agent}', resolve(auth, h, person, agent)))
                seen.add(h)
    return out


def account_line(auth, agent, svc, person):
    if svc == 'browser':
        try:
            return browser_profile(auth, agent)[0] + ('' if auth['grants'].get(agent, {}).get('browser') or
                                                       auth['grants'].get(f'{agent}@{person}', {}).get('browser')
                                                       else '  (its own, made on first use)')
        except SystemExit:
            return 'LEFT OUT: ' + granted(auth, agent, 'browser', person)[1]
    profile, why, refused = granted(auth, agent, svc, person)
    if refused:
        return 'LEFT OUT: ' + why.split(' (')[0]
    if not profile:
        return 'no grant'
    mine = auth['grants'].get(f'{agent}@{person}', {}).get(svc) == profile
    whose = owner_of(auth, profile)
    lent = person in auth['profiles'].get(profile, {}).get('with', [])
    return profile + ('  (their own)' if mine else f'  ({whose}\'s, shared with them)' if whose and lent
                      else f'  ({whose}\'s)' if whose else '  (shared)')


def cmd_people(args):
    auth = load_auth()
    if not auth['people']:
        print('no people yet: hq-auth person <you> name=.. owner, then hq-auth person <id> for each other person')
        return
    if '--matrix' in args:
        return matrix(auth)
    full = bool(args)
    order = sorted(auth['people'], key=lambda p: (not auth['people'][p].get('owner'), p))
    for pid in args or order:
        need_person(auth, pid)
        os.environ['HQ_PERSON'] = pid                      # browser_profile and settings read it
        p = auth['people'][pid]
        extra = ', '.join([f'{k} {p[k]}' for k in ('name', 'lang', 'tz') if p.get(k)]
                          + ([f'formerly {",".join(p["was"])}'] if p.get('was') else []))
        print(f'{pid}{"  (owner)" if p.get("owner") else ""}{"  · " + extra if extra else ""}')
        handles = ', '.join(f'{plat} {uid}' for plat, uid in sorted(p.get('handles', {}).items()))
        hint = f'hq-auth handle {pid} <platform> <user-id>' if p.get('owner') else f'hq-auth invite {pid}'
        print(f'  {"accounts":<9} {handles or "none linked (" + hint + ")"}')
        owns = sorted(n for n in auth['profiles'] if owner_of(auth, n) in (pid, 'the owner' if p.get('owner') else pid))
        if owns:
            print(f'  {"owns":<9} {", ".join(owns)}')
        reach = access(auth, pid)
        if p.get('owner') and not full:
            print(f'  {"agents":<9} all {len(reach)} (owner; hq-auth people {pid} for each one\'s accounts)')
            print()
            continue
        if not reach:
            print(f'  {"agents":<9} none (hq-auth member <agent> {pid})')
        for agent, how, r in reach:
            bits = [] if how == 'owner' else [r['preset'], r['mode']]
            bits += [f'deny {",".join(r["deny"])}'] if r.get('deny') else []
            bits += [f'model {r["model"]}'] if r.get('model') else []
            bits += [f'budget ${r["budget"]}/month'] if r.get('budget') and not how.startswith('helper') else []
            bits += [f'helpers {",".join(r["helpers"])}'] if r.get('helpers') and not how.startswith('helper') else []
            bits += [f'{k}={v}' for k, v in r.get('env', {}).items()]
            tag = '' if how in ('own', 'owner') else f'  [{how}]'
            print(f'  {agent:<9} {" · ".join(bits)}{tag}'.rstrip())
            for svc in services_of(auth, agent, pid):
                print(f'  {"":<9}   {svc:<12} {account_line(auth, agent, svc, pid)}')
        print()


def matrix(auth):
    """Agents down, people across: how each person reaches each agent."""
    order = sorted(auth['people'], key=lambda p: (not auth['people'][p].get('owner'), p))
    cells = {}
    for pid in order:
        for agent, how, r in access(auth, pid):
            cells[agent, pid] = 'owner' if how == 'owner' else \
                (r['preset'] + ('*' if how == 'everyone' else '') if not how.startswith('helper') else 'helper')
    width = max([len(p) for p in order] + [7]) + 2
    print(f'{"":<18}' + ''.join(f'{p:<{width}}' for p in order))
    for agent in agents():
        print(f'{agent:<18}' + ''.join(f'{cells.get((agent, p), "-"):<{width}}' for p in order))
    print('\n* from the everyone row · helper: only when called by an agent that lists it · - no access')


def cmd_person(args):
    if not args:
        die('person <id> [name=.. lang=.. tz=.. owner] [--rm]', 2)
    pid, (kv, flags) = args[0], pairs(args[1:], {'name', 'lang', 'tz', 'id'})
    if not re.fullmatch(r'[a-z][a-z0-9-]*', pid):
        die('a person id is lowercase letters, digits and -, e.g. sam', 2)
    auth = load_auth()
    if 'id' in kv:
        return rename(auth, pid, kv.pop('id'))
    if '--rm' in flags:
        auth['people'].pop(pid, None)
        for rows in auth['members'].values():
            rows.pop(pid, None)
        auth['members'] = {a: r for a, r in auth['members'].items() if r}
        auth['grants'] = {k: g for k, g in auth['grants'].items() if not k.endswith(f'@{pid}')}
        save_auth(auth)
        print(f'{pid} removed, with their memberships and grants (profiles they own are kept)')
        return
    if pid not in auth['people'] and canonical(auth, pid) != pid:
        die(f"'{pid}' was renamed to {canonical(auth, pid)}")
    p = auth['people'].setdefault(pid, {})
    p.update({k: v for k, v in kv.items() if v})
    for k in [k for k, v in kv.items() if not v]:
        p.pop(k, None)
    if 'owner' in flags:
        was = owner(auth)
        if was and was != pid:   # the old owner's logins stay theirs: pin the ones that were theirs by default
            pinned = [n for n, prof in auth['profiles'].items() if not prof.get('person') and owner_of(auth, n)]
            for n in pinned:
                auth['profiles'][n]['person'] = was
            if pinned:
                print(f'kept {was}\'s: {", ".join(sorted(pinned))} (hq-auth owner <profile> {pid} to hand one over)')
            print(f'note: anyone using this Mac account, and {was}\'s HQ_DISCORD_OWNER_ID, still run as the owner')
        for other in auth['people'].values():
            other.pop('owner', None)
        p['owner'] = True
    save_auth(auth)
    print(f'{pid}: ' + (', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k, v in p.items() if k not in ('handles', 'was')) or 'added'))


def rename(auth, old, new):
    """A person's new id, carried through every table that names them. The old id stays in `was`, so what outside
    auth.json still says old (a bridge thread they started, the cost ledger) keeps meaning them."""
    need_person(auth, old)
    if not re.fullmatch(r'[a-z][a-z0-9-]*', new):
        die('a person id is lowercase letters, digits and -, e.g. sam', 2)
    if new in auth['people'] or any(new in p.get('was', []) for p in auth['people'].values()):
        die(f"'{new}' is already a person (or one's old id)")
    p = auth['people'].pop(old)
    p['was'] = list(dict.fromkeys(p.get('was', []) + [old]))
    auth['people'][new] = p
    for rows in auth['members'].values():
        if old in rows:
            rows[new] = rows.pop(old)
    auth['grants'] = {(k.rsplit('@', 1)[0] + '@' + new if k.endswith(f'@{old}') else k): g
                      for k, g in auth['grants'].items()}
    owned = [n for n, prof in auth['profiles'].items() if prof.get('person') == old]
    for n in owned:
        auth['profiles'][n]['person'] = new
    for prof in auth['profiles'].values():
        if old in prof.get('with', []):
            prof['with'] = [new if x == old else x for x in prof['with']]
    for inv in auth['invites'].values():
        if inv.get('person') == old:
            inv['person'] = new
    save_auth(auth)
    print(f'{old} is now {new}' + (f'; owns {", ".join(sorted(owned))}' if owned else '')
          + ' (profile names stay as they are: they name accounts, not people)')


def canonical(auth, pid):
    """The person's id now, for an id that may be an old one."""
    if pid in auth['people']:
        return pid
    return next((p for p, v in auth['people'].items() if pid in v.get('was', [])), pid)


def cmd_handle(args):
    if len(args) != 3:
        die('handle <id> <platform> <user-id> | handle <id> <platform> --rm', 2)
    pid, plat, uid = args
    auth = load_auth()
    need_person(auth, pid)
    if uid == '--rm':
        auth['people'][pid].get('handles', {}).pop(plat, None)
        save_auth(auth)
        print(f'{pid}: no {plat} account')
        return
    bind(auth, pid, plat, uid)
    save_auth(auth)
    print(f'{pid} is {plat} {uid}')


def bind(auth, pid, plat, uid):
    if not re.fullmatch(r'-?\d+|[A-Z0-9]+', uid):
        die(f'{plat} user ids are numbers (Telegram, Discord) or Slack ids like U0123ABC, not usernames', 2)
    for other, p in auth['people'].items():
        if other != pid and p.get('handles', {}).get(plat) == uid:
            die(f'{plat} {uid} is already {other}')
    auth['people'][pid].setdefault('handles', {})[plat] = uid


def cmd_whois(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die('whois <platform> <user-id>', 2)
    auth = load_auth()
    for pid, p in auth['people'].items():
        if p.get('handles', {}).get(args[0]) == args[1]:
            print(pid)
            return
    sys.exit(1)


def cmd_who(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die('who <platform> <user-id>', 2)
    auth = load_auth()
    pid = next((p for p, v in auth['people'].items() if v.get('handles', {}).get(args[0]) == args[1]), None)
    me = owner(auth)
    print(json.dumps({'person': pid, 'owner': bool(pid) and is_owner(auth, pid),
                      'was': auth['people'][pid].get('was', []) if pid else [], 'owner_id': me,
                      'owner_linked': bool(me and auth['people'][me].get('handles', {}).get(args[0]))}))


def cmd_invite(args):
    if len(args) not in (1, 2):
        die('invite <id> [minutes]', 2)
    auth = load_auth()
    need_person(auth, args[0])
    minutes = int(args[1]) if len(args) == 2 else 15
    alphabet = 'ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789'   # no 0/O or 1/I to misread
    code = ''.join(alphabet[b % len(alphabet)] for b in os.urandom(6))
    auth['invites'][code] = {'person': args[0], 'expires': time.time() + minutes * 60}
    save_auth(auth)
    print(f'{code}\n{args[0]} sends "/link {code}" to the hq bot on any platform within {minutes} minutes')


def cmd_link(args):
    if len(args) != 3:
        die('link <platform> <user-id> <code>', 2)
    plat, uid, code = args
    auth = load_auth()
    inv = auth['invites'].pop(code.strip().upper(), None)
    if not inv or inv['expires'] < time.time():
        save_auth(auth)
        die('that code is unknown or expired; ask for a new one (hq-auth invite <id>)')
    bind(auth, inv['person'], plat, uid)
    save_auth(auth)
    print(inv['person'])


def cmd_preset(args):
    if not args:
        die('preset <name> [mode=.. deny=a,b] [--rm]', 2)
    name, (kv, flags) = args[0], pairs(args[1:], {'mode', 'deny'})
    auth = load_auth()
    if '--rm' in flags:
        auth['presets'].pop(name, None)
    else:
        p = auth['presets'].setdefault(name, dict(PRESETS.get(name, {})))
        if 'mode' in kv:
            check_free_shell(kv['mode'], flags, f'preset {name}')
            p['mode'] = kv['mode']
            p.pop('trusted', None)
            if kv['mode'] in FREE_SHELL:
                p['trusted'] = True
        if 'deny' in kv:
            p['deny'] = [d for d in kv['deny'].split(',') if d]
    save_auth(auth)
    print(f'{name}: {json.dumps(preset(auth, name)) if name in auth["presets"] or name in PRESETS else "removed"}')


def cmd_member(args):
    if len(args) < 2:
        die('member <agent>[,..] <id> [preset=.. mode=.. deny=.. model=.. helpers=a,b budget=USD env.VAR=..] [--trusted] [--rm]', 2)
    names, pid = [a for a in args[0].split(',') if a], args[1]
    kv, flags = pairs(args[2:], {'preset', 'mode', 'deny', 'model', 'helpers', 'budget', 'env.'})
    if kv.get('budget'):
        try:
            if float(kv['budget']) < 0:
                raise ValueError
        except ValueError:
            die('budget is dollars a month, e.g. budget=20', 2)
    auth = load_auth()
    if pid != EVERYONE:
        need_person(auth, pid)
    for agent in names:
        if agent not in agent_dirs():
            die(f"no agent '{agent}' (hq ls)")
        if '--rm' in flags:
            auth['members'].get(agent, {}).pop(pid, None)
            if not auth['members'].get(agent):
                auth['members'].pop(agent, None)
            print(f'{pid} may no longer use {agent}')
            continue
        if kv.get('mode'):
            check_free_shell(kv['mode'], flags, f'{pid} on {agent}')
        row = auth['members'].setdefault(agent, {}).setdefault(pid, {})
        if 'mode' in kv:
            row.pop('trusted', None)
            if kv['mode'] in FREE_SHELL:
                row['trusted'] = True
        for k, v in kv.items():
            if k.startswith('env.'):
                env = row.setdefault('env', {})
                env.update({k[4:]: v}) if v else env.pop(k[4:], None)
                if not env:
                    row.pop('env')
            elif k in ('deny', 'helpers'):
                row[k] = [x for x in v.split(',') if x]
            elif v:
                row[k] = v
            else:
                row.pop(k, None)
        if 'preset' in row:
            preset(auth, row['preset'])
        if pid == EVERYONE:
            p = preset(auth, row.get('preset', 'guest'))
            r = {'preset': row.get('preset', 'guest'), 'mode': mode_of(row, p),
                 'deny': p.get('deny', []) + row.get('deny', []), 'helpers': row.get('helpers', [])}
        else:
            r = resolve(auth, agent, pid)
        print(f'{"everyone hq knows" if pid == EVERYONE else pid} may use {agent}: preset {r["preset"]}, mode {r["mode"]}'
              + (f', deny {",".join(r["deny"])}' if r['deny'] else '')
              + (f', helpers {",".join(r["helpers"])}' if r['helpers'] else '')
              + (f', budget ${r["budget"]}/month' if r.get('budget') else '')
              + (' (a free shell on this Mac: trusted)' if r['mode'] in FREE_SHELL else ''))
    save_auth(auth)


def cmd_owner(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die('owner <profile> <id>|-|default', 2)
    prof, pid = args
    auth = load_auth()
    if prof not in auth['profiles']:
        die(f"no profile '{prof}'")
    if pid == '-':
        auth['profiles'][prof]['person'] = SHARED
    elif pid == 'default':
        auth['profiles'][prof].pop('person', None)
    else:
        need_person(auth, pid)
        auth['profiles'][prof]['person'] = pid
    save_auth(auth)
    who = owner_of(auth, prof)
    print(f'{prof}: ' + (f'{who}\'s; runs for anyone else never get it' if who else 'shared with everyone who may use '
                         'the agents granted it') + (' (the default for its service)' if pid == 'default' else ''))


def cmd_share(args):
    if len(args) not in (2, 3) or (len(args) == 3 and args[2] != '--rm'):
        die('share <profile> <id>[,..] [--rm]', 2)
    prof, ids = args[0], [i for i in args[1].split(',') if i]
    auth = load_auth()
    if prof not in auth['profiles']:
        die(f"no profile '{prof}'")
    for pid in ids:
        need_person(auth, pid)
    p = auth['profiles'][prof]
    lent = [x for x in p.get('with', []) if x not in ids] if len(args) == 3 else list(dict.fromkeys(p.get('with', []) + ids))
    if lent:
        p['with'] = lent
    else:
        p.pop('with', None)
    save_auth(auth)
    who = owner_of(auth, prof)
    print(f'{prof}: {who or "shared"}\'s' + (f', shared with {", ".join(lent)}' if lent else ', shared with no one else'))


def take_opts(args, names):
    opts, rest = {}, []
    it = iter(args)
    for a in it:
        if a in names:
            opts[a] = next(it, '')
        else:
            rest.append(a)
    return opts, rest


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ('-h', '--help'):
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return
    cmd, rest = argv[0], argv[1:]
    if cmd == 'ls':
        cmd_ls()
    elif cmd == 'grant' and len(rest) == 3:
        who, svc, profile = rest
        service(svc)
        # agent@person: that person's own account for the agent (tried first in their runs)
        base = lambda a: a.split('@', 1)[0]
        uses = (lambda a: uses_browser(base(a))) if svc == 'browser' else (lambda a: svc in needs(base(a)))
        names = [a for a in agents() if uses(a)] if who == '--all' else [a for a in who.split(',') if a]
        if not names:
            die(f'no agent lists {svc} in its needs' if who == '--all' else 'no agent named', 2)
        auth = load_auth()
        for a in names:
            if '@' in a:
                need_person(auth, a.split('@', 1)[1])
        profiles = [p for p in profile.split(',') if p]
        if any(not p.startswith(svc + '/') for p in profiles):
            die(f'a {svc} grant takes {svc}/<account> profiles', 2)
        for p in profiles:
            auth['profiles'].setdefault(p, {})
        for agent in names:
            auth['grants'].setdefault(agent, {})[svc] = profiles if len(profiles) > 1 else profiles[0]
        save_auth(auth)
        for agent in names:
            print(f'{agent} may use {svc} as {", ".join(profiles)}' + ('' if uses(agent) or agent == 'bridge'
                                                                       else f' (not in its needs yet)'))
    elif cmd == 'revoke' and len(rest) == 2:
        auth = load_auth()
        auth['grants'].get(rest[0], {}).pop(rest[1], None)
        save_auth(auth)
        print(f'{rest[0]} may no longer use {rest[1]}')
    elif cmd == 'set' and len(rest) == 2:
        cmd_set(*rest)
    elif cmd == 'env' and len(rest) >= 2:
        agent, svc, pairs = rest[0], rest[1], rest[2:]
        service(svc)
        auth = load_auth()
        mine = auth['env'].setdefault(agent, {}).setdefault(svc, {})
        for pair in pairs:
            var, eq, value = pair.partition('=')
            if not eq or not var:
                die(f'expected VAR=value, got {pair!r}', 2)
            if value:
                mine[var] = value
            else:
                mine.pop(var, None)
        if not mine:
            auth['env'][agent].pop(svc)
        if not auth['env'][agent]:
            auth['env'].pop(agent)
        if pairs:
            save_auth(auth)
        for var, value in settings(auth, agent, svc).items():
            print(f'{var}={value}')
    elif cmd == 'browser' and len(rest) in (1, 2):
        name = rest[0] if rest[0].startswith('browser/') else f'browser/{rest[0]}'
        auth = load_auth()
        prof = auth['profiles'].setdefault(name, {})
        if len(rest) == 2:
            if prof.get('browser') and prof['browser'] != rest[1]:
                print(f'note: {name} was made in {prof["browser"]}; its logins may not open in {rest[1]}',
                      file=sys.stderr)
            prof['browser'] = rest[1]
        save_auth(auth)
        folder = paths()['HQ_MACHINE'] / 'browsers' / name.split('/', 1)[1]
        users = [a for a, g in auth['grants'].items() if g.get('browser') == name]
        print(f'{name}: {prof.get("browser") or "browser not set (the first tool to open it picks)"}, {folder}'
              + (f'; granted to {", ".join(users)}' if users else ''))
    elif cmd == 'people':
        cmd_people(rest)
    elif cmd == 'person':
        cmd_person(rest)
    elif cmd == 'handle':
        cmd_handle(rest)
    elif cmd == 'whois':
        cmd_whois(rest)
    elif cmd == 'who':
        cmd_who(rest)
    elif cmd == 'invite':
        cmd_invite(rest)
    elif cmd == 'link':
        cmd_link(rest)
    elif cmd == 'preset':
        cmd_preset(rest)
    elif cmd == 'member':
        cmd_member(rest)
    elif cmd == 'owner':
        cmd_owner(rest)
    elif cmd == 'share':
        cmd_share(rest)
    elif cmd in ('may', 'resolve'):
        opts, rest = take_opts(rest, {'--via', '--person'})
        auth = load_auth()
        if cmd == 'may' and len(rest) == 2:
            ok, why = may(auth, rest[0], rest[1], opts.get('--via'))
            print(why)
            sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)
        if cmd == 'resolve' and len(rest) == 1:
            person = opts.get('--person') or acting(auth)
            print(json.dumps(resolve(auth, rest[0], person, opts.get('--via') or None)))
            return
        die(f'{cmd}: see hq-auth --help', 2)
    elif cmd == 'mcp-config' and len(rest) == 1:
        cmd_mcp_config(rest[0])
    elif cmd == 'exec':
        cmd_exec(rest)
    elif cmd == 'get':
        cmd_get(rest)
    elif cmd == 'granted':
        agent, rest = take_for(rest)
        if len(rest) != 1:
            die('granted [--for AGENT] <service>', 2)
        g = load_auth()['grants'].get(agent, {}).get(rest[0])
        print('\n'.join(g if isinstance(g, list) else [g] if g else []))
    else:
        die(f'unknown command: {" ".join(argv)} (hq-auth --help)', 2)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main(sys.argv[1:])
